# Context, Scope & Execution

**Context:** Use ONLY files explicitly named. No scanning/inferring. Additional files → ask first. Missing context → STOP.

**Scope:** Smallest possible scope. No refactoring unrelated code. No project-wide changes without explicit approval.

**Large pastes / input:** Pasted content (project overviews, module lists, long logs, multi-file dumps) is REFERENCE only. MUST NOT treat it as "context to act on." If the paste is large or implies scanning multiple files → **STOP and ask**: "This appears to reference many modules/files. Please specify the exact scope you want me to work on (file, module, or discrete task)." MUST NOT automatically process all of it.

**Automation:** MUST NOT run agents, chains, background steps, or multi-step actions automatically unless explicitly requested.

**Commands:** Cursor MUST NOT execute ANY command. No git, gradle, aws, npm, maven, docker, migrations, builds, scripts, or any shell/terminal command. Cursor MAY ONLY provide the command as plain text, labeled "Command to run manually," for the user to execute. MUST NEVER run, simulate, or claim a command was executed.
